ethod lines are supported by1012480:1–2 and the complete もう body; comparison is required, not unrestricted synonymy.\n\n## Findings\n1. MAJOR / C2 / words\\先.md:9; words\\向こう.md:4,9,16–24.\nActual captions: 先 “впереди; раньше; в будущем”; 向こう “там; по ту сторону”. Neither guard list contains the other. Complete JMdict1387210:4 gives 先 spatial ahead/beyond; complete1277140:2 independently gives 向こう ahead/beyond. New “впереди” can fit the other Japanese candidate; the old far-side caption intersects the qualified beyond sense. This is direct evidence, not inference through shared ほか/他 exclusions or merely a “place” component.\nConsequence: a defensible spatial answer remains an allegedly wrong distractor. Fix: add the conservative direct guard on new 先; bind this existing provider and complete object/body evidence in an honest subsequent amendment, then focused acceptance follow-up. No new provider/baseline edit. Confidence HIGH for omission and dictionary/context overlap; no frequency statistic claimed.\n\n2. MEDIUM / C2 / words\\初めて.md:9; words\\初め.md:9; words\\先.md:9; candidate proposals50–52,54.\nConsequential acceptance qualifications, not proven mistranslations:\n- 50 初めて–最初 (“впервые” / “начало; первый”) and51 初めて–いちばん (“впервые” / “первый; самый”):1342550:1,3 supports first experience/one's first;1293990:1 and1165970:1 support beginning/order. An implied noun does not establish that the isolated ordinary ordinal answer tests first-ever experience. Bare-prompt necessity UNVERIFIED.\n- 52 初め–初めて (“начало; поначалу” / “впервые”):2646830:1 expressly restricts suffixぞめ to after a verb'sます-stem. It does not license unrestricted standalone はじめ=впервые. Conservative suffix protection is possible; ordinary bare-prompt applicability UNVERIFIED.\n- 54 先–宛名 (“впереди; раньше; в будущем” / “имя и адрес получателя”):1387210:7,9 and1586520:1 establish qualified address/recipient overlap, not that bare先 denotes the entire joint name-and-address caption. That stronger answer-fit/necessity UNVERIFIED.\nConsequence if rubberstamped: over-exclusion/unsupported ordinary equivalence claims. Needed: modern independently attested constructions, readings and exact Russian renderings, plus an explicit rule connecting them to bare quiz choices; otherwise retain declared conservative over-protection, not proven necessity. Reject unrestricted equivalence claims, not attested senses. Confidence HIGH in these evidence limits; no automatic deletion demanded.\n\n3. MEDIUM / evidence provenance/C2 auditability / docs\\translation-batches\\046-time-sequence-positions-source-adjudication.json:2989–3004.\nAll three recorded workingRawSha256 values disagree with actual frozen source working/Git bytes; CRLF projections do not explain them. rubrics[0:1],[1:2],[2:3] therefore failed before returning content. Complete blobs were recovered read-only at the required commit; working bytes matched Git exactly. Actual RAW SHA256, accuracy/consistency/comprehension respectively:\nf839076113f2b3f3928676277f1a36a629f271d158e1d62eb665864944e31544\ndf817ab7bd6abbdd0182b3e5db1ec3871ed0766ebdf4d63e3aba69c0ca7d6b1f\n62178bbedd8eb2c8008820abfac331e7902d6b30893f41d46c66cd0626be2ed3\nConsequence: rubric provenance binding is not reproducible, although substantive reading succeeded. Fix: append corrected exact-commit/domain binding; investigate mismatch without rewriting immutable receipts. Confidence HIGH; historical cause UNKNOWN.\n\n## Individual guard adjudication\nZero-based IDs0–49 and53: supported as qualified conservative dictionary/context protections, NOT proved ordinary-frequency necessities. Independent grounds:\n0–1 month duration/alternate一月 reading;2–9 今 immediate/additional/current-period/current-occasion senses, 今日 restricted toこんにち;10–12 shared beginning lemma/最初;13–14 beginnings versus頭 beginning/linear head;15–16 一 beginning sense4;17–18 first-in-line, retaining “esp.初め”;19–20 journey outset, not invented generic出発 sense;21 先–前 direct spatial/earlier overlap;22–23 priority/order;24 linear front/head;25 former, not elderly;26–27 destination/address/place;28–29 前 attributive first-part only;30 linear front/head;31 former, not every old object;32–35 linear starting end, supported by Russian начало sense2, not every commencement;36 remaining material, not sound alone;37–38 remainder/rest including他's separateほか reading;39–40 additional quantity;41 addition;42–44 sequential/additive use, not causal/noun-listing “and”;45 後のち future, not free reading substitution;46 next occasion;47 half with attachment distinctions;48–49 remaining continuation/other party;53 今–もう now/imminence, independently supported by1012480 and taxi context. Decisions50–52,54: UNVERIFIED as above. Source 後–後ろ: preserved/supported by1269410/1269320. No transitive exclusions adopted.\n\n## Optional\nNo stylistic changes requested. Optional navigation does not recursively force providers; shared components alone do not justify guards.\n\n## Limits and follow-up\nFurther dictionary-only risks are not silently cleared: 先–最近 (“впереди; раньше; в будущем” / “недавно; в последнее время”) and 今–先 (“сейчас” / that先 caption), through1005180's explicitly rare written先/さっき “a short while ago/just now” and corresponding temporal senses. Contemporary written use and bare-prompt reading policy are needed; ordinary necessity remains UNVERIFIED, not an automatic rare-reading clique.\nOriginal53-proposal freeze74a742c and amendment082a655 are distinct: amendment followed16 bodies but preceded its two extra metadata guards. No backdated freeze claim. Hash checks/author tests are not semantic/native-effectiveness proof. Russian primary captures are derived text, not rawHTML/HTTP200/network proof.\nNo writes/artifacts, agents/contacts, validators/tests/builds, external services, media operations or concurrent checkout access. No new runtime activation/device/IME/media/native approval. Historical grammar/counter/picture and five genuinely unlocked Word Type native passes remain